      "body": "## Purpose\n\nAddresses Bug3 in #56251.\n\n`MultiprocExecutor.collective_rpc()` checks `is_failed` before serializing\ncallable RPCs. If a worker fails during serialization, the monitor thread can\nshut down the executor and clear `rpc_broadcast_mq`. The RPC then attempts to\ncall `enqueue()` on `None`, producing a misleading `AttributeError`.\n\nThis change snapshots and rechecks the broadcast queue after serialization,\nso this race follows the existing `RuntimeError(\"Executor failed.\")` failure\ncontract.\n\nThis does not duplicate existing work: #56282 addresses Bug1, #56336\naddresses Bug2, and #56854 addresses Bug5. No open PR addressing Bug3 was\nfound.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- Add a deterministic CPU-only regression test that pauses callable\n  serialization, shuts down the executor, and then resumes the RPC.\n- Verify that the old implementation raises `AttributeError`.\n- Verify that the fixed implementation raises `RuntimeError`.\n- Run the executor unit tests and applicable lint/type checks.\n\n## Test Result\n\nBefore the fix:\n\n```text\nFAILED test_collective_rpc_fails_cleanly_if_shutdown_during_serialization\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'enqueue'\n```\n\nAfter the fix:\n\n```text\ntests/v1/executor/test_multiproc_executor.py:\n3 passed\n\ntests/v1/executor/test_executor.py\n-k 'supports_async_scheduling or worker_termination_timeout':\n6 passed, 5 deselected\n```\n\nRuff check/format, typos, mypy, SPDX, and applicable local checks passed.\n\nThe complete pre-commit run was blocked by an unrelated ShellCheck binary\ndownload failure in the test environment.\n\nModel evaluation: Not applicable. This change only normalizes an executor\nshutdown error path and does not affect model output or accuracy.\n\n## AI Assistance\n\nOpenAI Codex assisted with investigation, implementation, and testing. The\nhuman contributor reviewed every changed line, understands the concurrency\nbehavior, reviewed the relevant test results, and is responsible for the\nsubmission.\n",
